@startuml signal-correlation
title US-06: Signal Correlation - Two Weak Signals Joined via proximity.candidates + Redis

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nalert-state:{id}" as AlertState
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

note over Evaluator
  Runs on Kafka consume from proximity.candidates.
  Only the elected leader emits alerts.
end note

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ entity_a_id, entity_b_id, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, distance_metres }

note over Evaluator
  Proximity candidate: unscheduled pair detected
  by the Correlation Worker.
  Known associates already filtered upstream -
  they never appear here.
  This is weak signal 2.
end note

Evaluator -> AlertState : GET alert-state:{entity_b_id}
AlertState --> Evaluator : $dark_since_ms (SIGNAL_LOSS alert active - Entity B is dark)

note over Evaluator
  Weak signal 1: active signal loss confirmed via alert-state key.
  dark_since_ms from the key value gives the start of the loss window.
  Not actionable on its own.
end note

Evaluator -> Evaluator : check: does proximity timestamp_ms\nfall within the signal loss window?

alt proximity within loss window
  Evaluator -> Neo4j : MATCH (b:Entity {id: $id_b})-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT]->(a:Entity {id: $id_a})\nWHERE e.timestamp_ms = $timestamp_ms\nRETURN e

  note over Neo4j
    Targeted lookup on a specific entity pair.
    Not a scan for recent edges -
    the candidate arrived via Kafka.
    Neo4j is queried only for relationship context
    needed to assemble the composite alert payload.
  end note

  Neo4j --> Evaluator : proximity event details { lat, lon, timestamp_ms, distance_metres }

  note over Evaluator
    Both weak signals confirmed.
    Together they form a composite pattern.
    Emit ONE composite alert at elevated priority.
  end note

  Evaluator -> Evaluator : correlate signals\n-> COMPOSITE alert at elevated priority
end

@enduml
